cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "apertus-eval-prep: evaluation configuration as part of the measurement"
message: If you use this harness or the committed run JSON, please cite it.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Bhandari
    given-names: Shivani
repository-code: https://github.com/Shivani767/apertus-eval-prep
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >
  Frozen-prompt generative exact-match harness that treats chat template,
  decoding backend, prompt, seed, and quantization as named OFAT factors.
  Committed findings (replayable JSON): omitting or mismatching the chat
  template moves a 28-item canary 71.4% → 53.6% → 42.9%; HF generate vs vLLM
  differs by 7.1 points on multilingual items; on SmolLM2-1.7B (n=800) a
  concise prompt drops accuracy 39.8% → 23.2% (Wilson CIs disjoint),
  concentrated on GSM8K/MGSM.
